MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CandleStore persists Candle data per (symbol, timeframe) using Python's
stdlib sqlite3 — no new dependency. PRIMARY KEY (symbol, timeframe,
time) plus INSERT OR REPLACE makes overlapping incremental saves
idempotent for free; no separate 'have I already got this candle'
check is needed at any call site.

API: save_candles (upsert), load_candles (range query), load_latest
(most-recent-N), get_coverage (earliest/latest cached time, used by
historical.py for staleness checks), count, validate (ordering, OHLC
sanity, gap detection — returns a CacheValidationResult rather than
raising, so a caller can inspect issues without crashing), and clear.

find_gaps() is a standalone function (not a CandleStore method) so gap
*detection* has exactly one implementation, shared by both
CandleStore.validate (report-only) and, in the next commit,
HistoricalDataService.fill_gaps (report-and-download).

data/types.py adds CacheValidationResult and SyncReport, the DTOs this
layer returns.

24 tests covering round-tripping, upsert/overlap behavior, symbol and
timeframe isolation, range queries, coverage, validation (clean data,
gaps, inverted OHLC), clearing, and cache-directory failure handling.
